{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 -c \\\"\nimport json\no=json.load(open('logs/c0f7723f05d8430aaf36bf2b4f9ce862/observations.json'))\nfor i,e in enumerate(o['events']):\n    if e.get('event','').startswith('verify_leader_nonvoter'):\n        print(i, e.get('variant'), {k:e.get(k) for k in ('voter_quorum','voter_reachable','nonvoter_reachable','verify_succeeded','verify_error','elapsed_ms','leader_state_after')})\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"22 slowed-timers {'voter_quorum': 2, 'voter_reachable': 'failed to connect to peer: 024620ae-41d6-9a7a-d389-c87248e53cd8', 'nonvoter_reachable': '<nil>', 'verify_succeeded': None, 'verify_error': None, 'elapsed_ms': None, 'leader_state_after': None}\n23 slowed-timers {'voter_quorum': 2, 'voter_reachable': None, 'nonvoter_reachable': None, 'verify_succeeded': True, 'verify_error': '<nil>', 'elapsed_ms': 0, 'leader_state_after': 'Leader'}\n24 default-timers {'voter_quorum': 2, 'voter_reachable': 'failed to connect to peer: 0a7ea836-bbab-eef0-c953-e0f886b4cac7', 'nonvoter_reachable': '<nil>', 'verify_succeeded': None, 'verify_error': None, 'elapsed_ms': None, 'leader_state_after': None}\n25 default-timers {'voter_quorum': 2, 'voter_reachable': None, 'nonvoter_reachable': None, 'verify_succeeded': True, 'verify_error': '<nil>', 'elapsed_ms': 0, 'leader_state_after': 'Leader'}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Read the retained receipt of the successor experiment 055ce90edba24e96b6cad538951eea1a-experiment (CheckRun c0f7723f05d8430aaf36bf2b4f9ce862, exit 0, 26 events). It runs the isolation case twice: events 22 and 23 are the slowed-timer case and events 24 and 25 the default-timer case, and both result events report verification succeeding with no error while only the non-voter is reachable. The account is updated to cite both receipts and the behavior entry is revised so the reproduced default-timer result replaces the caveat about artificially slowed timers.\\\",\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"97b6ea8503a34f9eacf83b6834071cc1-knowledge-0\\\",\n   \\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n   \\\"statement\\\":\\\"Leader verification counts acknowledgements from non-voters: with the voter quorum unreachable and one non-voter reachable, VerifyLeader returned success with no error while the node remained leader, both with slowed timers and with the repository's default in-memory timers, because verifyLeader registers its future with every entry of the replication map and that map is built for every server in the configuration, including non-voters.\\\",\n   \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"A configuration with more voters than the reachable set and at least one reachable non-voter; the leader can reach the non-voter but not a quorum of voters; the verification is issued before the leader lease steps the leader down.\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-verifyleader\\\",\\\"s-replstate\\\",\\\"s-heartbeat\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"5e092a2b160b4a2f955d48ee6fa06ad9\\\":[23],\\\"c0f7723f05d8430aaf36bf2b4f9ce862\\\":[23,25]},\n   \\\"changed_premise\\\":\\\"The first revision recorded the behaviour only for a cluster with slowed timers; the successor run measures the same isolation with the library's default in-memory timers and reports the same result, so the behaviour is stated for both timer configurations instead of carrying the caveat.\\\"}\n ],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[\n  {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"790eb5d64ed94ef5aea4736e6f66381d-question-0\\\",\n   \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"055ce90edba24e96b6cad538951eea1a-experiment\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-verifyleader\\\",\\\"s-replstate\\\",\\\"s-heartbeat\\\",\\\"s-lease\\\",\\\"s-quorum\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"c0f7723f05d8430aaf36bf2b4f9ce862\\\":[22,23,24,25],\\\"5e092a2b160b4a2f955d48ee6fa06ad9\\\":[22,23]},\n   \\\"joint_history\\\":\\\"Two receipts answer this question. The first (5e092a2b160b4a2f955d48ee6fa06ad9 at indices 22 and 23) measured the isolation with slowed timers; the successor (c0f7723f05d8430aaf36bf2b4f9ce862) runs the same scenario twice in one file, at indices 22 and 23 with slowed timers and at indices 24 and 25 with the library's default in-memory timers, each emitting its own variant.\\\",\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Current account: the leader-verification quorum can be satisfied without a voter quorum, and the successor run shows this is not an artifact of slack timers. Evidence per case: the slowed-timer setup event 22 records three voters with a quorum of two, a direct AppendEntries to a voter failing with a connection error and one to the non-voter succeeding, and its result event 23 records success in under a millisecond with no error while the node stayed Leader; the default-timer setup event 24 records the same premise with the library's own timers and its result event 25 records the same outcome, success with no error in under a millisecond and the node still Leader. Both declared comparisons are violated, at indices 23 and 25 respectively. Mechanism from source: verifyLeader starts its count at one for itself and registers the future in every entry of the leader's replication map, which startStopReplication builds for every server of the configuration except the leader without filtering by suffrage; each peer's heartbeat acknowledges the pending verification when its AppendEntries succeeds, so a non-voter's acknowledgement can raise the count to the voter quorum that quorumSize computes from voters alone. Bound from source: the leader lease counts only voters, so the node steps down within LeaderLeaseTimeout of losing the voter quorum; the exposure is the interval before that check, and the default-timer case shows the verification completes inside it. Consequence: a client that uses VerifyLeader to guard against stale reads can be told the node is still verified while every voter is unreachable, which is the situation the call is documented to detect.\\\",\n   \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n   \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n   \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n    \\\"The leader lease still counts voters only, so the node steps down shortly after and the incorrect verification result is bounded by that interval rather than persisting.\\\",\n    \\\"The defect requires a configuration that has non-voters at all; a cluster of voters only cannot exhibit it, because every replication peer is then a voter and the acknowledgement set equals the voter set.\\\",\n    \\\"No write path is affected: entry commitment uses the commitment map, which contains voters only, so this is a read-verification path rather than a commit-rule path.\\\",\n    \\\"The default-timer case still isolates the leader immediately before the verification, so the observation covers the interval in which a client would call VerifyLeader after losing the voter quorum, not a steady state.\\\"\n   ],\n   \\\"limitations\\\":[\n    \\\"Measured on four-peer in-memory clusters with the repository's own facilities; production timings and transports are not covered.\\\",\n    \\\"The probe issued the verification directly rather than through an application that then serves a read, so the stale-read consequence is inferred from the documented purpose of the API rather than measured end to end.\\\",\n    \\\"Both cases isolate the leader by transport disconnection and confirm it with direct AppendEntries attempts recorded in the same events.\\\"\n   ]}\n ]\n}\njson.dump(u,open('update.json','w'),indent=2); print('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
